{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1005543-z-splat-books","id":1005543,"title":"Z-splat books","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-19T19:28:04-08:00","id":1005543,"title":"Z-splat books","content":"This is no biggie. No huge topic in any way... But... I have thought a bit about this and come to realize I would very much like to see Z-splat books for the updated CofD game lines. I would most certainly buy a book full of only Bloodlines, Lodges, or Legacies. The stories behind them are interesting to read, and the more examples one gets, the easier it is to design stuff on ones own, I think.<br /> <br /> Would it be possible for such books to be made for 2e?<br /> This isn't exactly a petition for it, I'm just curious as to if it could get made.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T21:05:07-08:00","id":1005578,"title":"","content":"I think a lot of us are hoping so. Though with the z-splats getting less coverage in the core books so far, I'm hoping that (at least the first round of) z-splat books use updating old examples to the new rules with explanations of the process to help with more guidance on building your own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T22:48:28-08:00","id":1005610,"title":"","content":"I admit, the only one I'd do is Entitlements and Eldritch Orders for Changeling. The rest, I never really got into.<br /> <br /> But as Entitlements go, I'd write, like, a fourth of a book of them, easily. Add their inherent weird factor in Changeling society and then factor in how much that society has changed in 2E, as well as a couple other points of weirdness, and yeah. We'd have fun.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Actually, with the way Lodges are,I'd be all over that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 11-22-2016, 03:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T00:54:34-08:00","id":1005639,"title":"","content":"I certainly hope some are coming. They have a tendency to be full of historical hooks, and historical worldbuilding is one of my favourite parts of CofD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T08:45:34-08:00","id":1005717,"title":"","content":"I'd love to see them make some z-splat books. I've always loved flipping through them and finding story hooks and character ideas for my games. I'd love to see a mix of updated ones and new ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T09:05:58-08:00","id":1005725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1005543-z-splat-books?p=1005639#post1005639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I certainly hope some are coming. They have a tendency to be full of historical hooks, and historical worldbuilding is one of my favourite parts of CofD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. It says so much about the world to get more information about specific groups and their history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T10:41:13-08:00","id":1005757,"title":"","content":"I know that there has been three updated bloodlines for Requiem, but other than that I mostly use fanwork for updated Z-splats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T11:07:29-08:00","id":1005766,"title":"","content":"I'm not big on just big books full of them; those end up feeling too much like D&amp;D's bloated sea of new spells and Prestige Classes back in 3.5. I'd much sooner see things like The Pack, which gave us five new Lodges but plenty else to offer, or getting one or two z-splats tossed into a given setting for Dark Eras.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T12:35:15-08:00","id":1005808,"title":"","content":"I think the desire for them not to just be in books like The Pack or Dark Eras, is that if you just want some neat z-splats, they get locked behind books with lots of other stuff. The big books of them (esp. since few of those are referenced in other books, making them extremely optional stuff) had an appeal to people in that way.<br /> <br /> A different approach are things like some of the later Night Horrors books: be a big book of them, but have clusters of linked groups that can be used as part of a bigger story rather than just a bunch of loosely thematically related ones, and even include groups from other game lines (like a new Hunter group that's linked in with the cluster) to expand things out.<br /> <br /> When executed well you have both a collection of functionally stand-alone z-splats, as well as something more engaging to do with the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T13:15:27-08:00","id":1005829,"title":"","content":"I personally prefer the &quot;book of many things including a few Z-splats&quot; approach over the &quot;book of many Z-splats&quot; approach. The latter is fine if you just want a ton of character options, but I prefer the former as it tends to be better rounded and have something for everyone. It also seems to be the preferred model at the moment, not just for CofD, but for the RPG industry as a whole, if we look at D&amp;D as the standard. The &quot;big book of splats&quot; model is a little 90s/00s.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T14:16:09-08:00","id":1005849,"title":"","content":"Hmm.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhat if, hear me out here and note that this is literally just off the top of my head and I have no influence over how OP does things, what if they were released singly as mini-pdfs; so, for example, rather than the Book of Lodges Take Three with twenty Lodges in it, the twenty Lodges (or Legacies or Bloodlines or what have you) were released as individual, very cheap pdfs? That way, you could just buy the ones you were interested in.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T14:23:01-08:00","id":1005853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1005543-z-splat-books?p=1005849#post1005849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhat if, hear me out here and note that this is literally just off the top of my head and I have no influence over how OP does things, what if they were released singly as mini-pdfs; so, for example, rather than the Book of Lodges Take Three with twenty Lodges in it, the twenty Lodges (or Legacies or Bloodlines or what have you) were released as individual, very cheap pdfs? That way, you could just buy the ones you were interested in.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd prefer them as one book, but what if OP did something similar to Dreamscarred Press and released the as both individual PDFs and an compilations?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T14:55:08-08:00","id":1005866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1005543-z-splat-books?p=1005849#post1005849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhat if, hear me out here and note that this is literally just off the top of my head and I have no influence over how OP does things, what if they were released singly as mini-pdfs; so, for example, rather than the Book of Lodges Take Three with twenty Lodges in it, the twenty Lodges (or Legacies or Bloodlines or what have you) were released as individual, very cheap pdfs? That way, you could just buy the ones you were interested in.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hell yeah, I'd be down with that. I mean, they were doing something similar with Requiem for a while, putting out short Bloodline writeups on the blog. I'd definitely pay a couple of bucks a pop for more of those.<br /> <br /> I mean, I'd also buy a big book 'o Bloodlines if they sold it. But this seems like a good way to get them out there without doing it that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T15:01:06-08:00","id":1005870,"title":"","content":"Yeah I think I'd prefer the individual z-splat pdfs route.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T15:28:46-08:00","id":1005882,"title":"","content":"I've advocated for it in the past as well. Release individual or small batches of z-splat pdfs, and have a compilation option (probably cheaper than buying each individually) for people that are going to be more collect-them-all minded, and that's enough material to justify PoD.<br /> <br /> Though I do think the Night Horrors books managed to do a decent job of something of a middle ground between &quot;big book of z-splats&quot; and, &quot;a few thematic extra z-splats related to the theme of the book.&quot; And I think 2e would benefit highly from books that go into more detail on custom z-splat building which is an opportunity to do some updating of old ones without it just being the &quot;big book&quot; thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T15:42:15-08:00","id":1005888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1005543-z-splat-books?p=1005808#post1005808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the desire for them not to just be in books like The Pack or Dark Eras, is that if you just want some neat z-splats, they get locked behind books with lots of other stuff. The big books of them (esp. since few of those are referenced in other books, making them extremely optional stuff) had an appeal to people in that way.<br /> <br /> A different approach are things like some of the later Night Horrors books: be a big book of them, but have clusters of linked groups that can be used as part of a bigger story rather than just a bunch of loosely thematically related ones, and even include groups from other game lines (like a new Hunter group that's linked in with the cluster) to expand things out.<br /> <br /> When executed well you have both a collection of functionally stand-alone z-splats, as well as something more engaging to do with the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Look at it this way: if I don't really care for z-splats and you love them above everything else, a book with a few z-splats along with some other content has stuff both of us want in it, and thus we'll both buy it. If a book consists entirely of z-splats, I'm not gonna buy it, while the hypothetical you here wouldn't buy the inverse. Ideally every book has at least one thing in it that everyone will want, so that the maximum number of people will pick it up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1005543-z-splat-books?p=1005849#post1005849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhat if, hear me out here and note that this is literally just off the top of my head and I have no influence over how OP does things, what if they were released singly as mini-pdfs; so, for example, rather than the Book of Lodges Take Three with twenty Lodges in it, the twenty Lodges (or Legacies or Bloodlines or what have you) were released as individual, very cheap pdfs? That way, you could just buy the ones you were interested in.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would be all for this, as the existing z-splat books seemed to largely be content I had zero interest in with a handful of super neat ones tossed in there every time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 11-20-2016, 06:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T16:07:37-08:00","id":1005894,"title":"","content":"I get the idea, but there's two issues with the &quot;some extra z-splats&quot; approach:<br /> <br /> 1) &quot;Having something for everyone&quot; doesn't always work, because it can also make people feel like they're only getting &quot;half&quot; of what they want, and having to pay for &quot;half&quot; of stuff they don't want when they could by a book that's almost all stuff they want. Maximizing buyers can be harmed if you try to appeal to everyone and end up appealing to no one.<br /> <br /> 2) A lot of the z-splats in the 1e &quot;big book&quot; approach books might have never happened without those books. Z-splat focused don't have to fit in to the themes and goals of a book that's focused on something else. This is why I keep going back to the Night Horrors series that managed to have a few z-splat focused books, that had a lot more story/flavor compared to the bigger books of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T16:22:46-08:00","id":1005897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1005543-z-splat-books?p=1005894#post1005894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) &quot;Having something for everyone&quot; doesn't always work, because it can also make people feel like they're only getting &quot;half&quot; of what they want, and having to pay for &quot;half&quot; of stuff they don't want when they could by a book that's almost all stuff they want. Maximizing buyers can be harmed if you try to appeal to everyone and end up appealing to no one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, as most of the z-splat books only have one or two entries that really interest me. But this isn't necessarily something OP has decided to avoid. Dark Eras, for instance, is a hefty book that has little to offer fans of Mummy, Vampire, or Promethean. Of course they made it up by offering to sell distinct sections on their own, at least in the Kickstarter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) A lot of the z-splats in the 1e &quot;big book&quot; approach books might have never happened without those books. Z-splat focused don't have to fit in to the themes and goals of a book that's focused on something else. This is why I keep going back to the Night Horrors series that managed to have a few z-splat focused books, that had a lot more story/flavor compared to the bigger books of them. </div> </div> </div>Yes, I think Night Horrors is a great line for adding miscellaneous things to the various lines in Chronicles of Darkness. Vampire has done the best, so far, as while one book was a more 'standard' first edition Night Horrors with mostly NPCs, though it contained some extra bloodlines, Disciplines and rituals, the other contained proto-Vampires, antagonists and draugr, strix, larva and dhampir. It's easy to imagine a second edition Night Horrors book containing domains, individual NPCs, covenants, a clan, bloodlines, and other odds and ends.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1005543-z-splat-books?p=1005849#post1005849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhat if, hear me out here and note that this is literally just off the top of my head and I have no influence over how OP does things, what if they were released singly as mini-pdfs; so, for example, rather than the Book of Lodges Take Three with twenty Lodges in it, the twenty Lodges (or Legacies or Bloodlines or what have you) were released as individual, very cheap pdfs? That way, you could just buy the ones you were interested in.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would like that, but I think there's a lot of people who balk at the idea of buying something that only exists in pdf format. This could be gone around by having a solid book that could be bought containing all the mini-pdfs, of course.<br /> <br /> I'm still for a gameline-oriented Patreon with updates and sneak peeks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-20-2016, 07:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T16:35:21-08:00","id":1005901,"title":"","content":"I should rephrase. I don't really care that the bit 'o this, bit o' that approach has something for everyone. I like it because it has a wide variety of things for me. Bloodlines or Lodges or whatever are great, but the big book o' Z-splats approach quickly leads to splat bloat. I would much rather have a few cool ones, a few new Merits, maybe a new optional subsystem or two, maybe a new power set, etc.<br /> <br /> That said, I'd still be all over the one-splat-mini-PDF approach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 11-20-2016, 08:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T21:48:59-08:00","id":1005977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1005543-z-splat-books?p=1005766#post1005766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not big on just big books full of them; those end up feeling too much like D&amp;D's bloated sea of new spells and Prestige Classes back in 3.5. I'd much sooner see things like The Pack, which gave us five new Lodges but plenty else to offer, or getting one or two z-splats tossed into a given setting for Dark Eras.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I always liked the huge sea of spells, feats, and prestige classes among other things- it gave a massive amount of flexibility and let you differentiate characters quite a bit. I suppose the mini pdf approaches would be okay, but I like collected in one spot type of things myself. I guess if they did it akin to Dragon Magazine, where you have a collected Annual at the end of each year, that might be more my style.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T08:04:34-08:00","id":1006195,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I prefer the books that have content that's spread across a few different ideas; books that have a little bit of everything make affording these books a lot easier than buying books full of one type of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T08:36:16-08:00","id":1006206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1005543-z-splat-books?p=1005897#post1005897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree, as most of the z-splat books only have one or two entries that really interest me. But this isn't necessarily something OP has decided to avoid. Dark Eras, for instance, is a hefty book that has little to offer fans of Mummy, Vampire, or Promethean. Of course they made it up by offering to sell distinct sections on their own, at least in the Kickstarter.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking that emulating Dark Eras would be exactly the way to go. One big book with chapters of thematic Z-splats for each line that also get sold separately as pdfs of the chapters. I think a Kickstarter of that could go very well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T01:16:52-08:00","id":1006629,"title":"","content":"Yeah, individually sold pdfs of z-splats, maybe with a cheaper option if you buy them in a bunddle. That would be great, anyone could have exactly what they wanted, no more, no less.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T02:56:58-08:00","id":1006637,"title":"","content":"I did have an idea for a new format of Legacy book that wasn't just a copy of Requiem's bloodline book format, but I have no idea if White Wolf liked it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T06:22:22-08:00","id":1006677,"title":"","content":"I also prefer a little bit of everything in a book, it expands the setting and the world in nice little ways. If I only get Z type book, then suddenly either I don't use most of the book, or there's an influx of Z splats in the setting. Now if the same book only has a couple Z splat things, alongside other things then the game expands in a more natural way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T07:06:48-08:00","id":1006692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1005543-z-splat-books?p=1005849#post1005849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhat if, hear me out here and note that this is literally just off the top of my head and I have no influence over how OP does things, what if they were released singly as mini-pdfs; so, for example, rather than the Book of Lodges Take Three with twenty Lodges in it, the twenty Lodges (or Legacies or Bloodlines or what have you) were released as individual, very cheap pdfs? That way, you could just buy the ones you were interested in.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>That'd be great actually. I'd certainly pay for individual bloodlines. I actually prefer browsing several smaller PDF's. Easier to cross-reference. So I'd be all for that.<br /> See if you can badger some higher-up to greenlight it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> There is one thing that's a problem here though: Vampire needs a bit of a guide on &quot;how to make a Bloodline&quot;.<br /> It'd need a The Pack equivalent first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T19:55:28-08:00","id":1006987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1005543-z-splat-books?p=1006692#post1006692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That'd be great actually. I'd certainly pay for individual bloodlines. I actually prefer browsing several smaller PDF's. Easier to cross-reference. So I'd be all for that.<br /> See if you can badger some higher-up to greenlight it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> There is one thing that's a problem here though: Vampire needs a bit of a guide on &quot;how to make a Bloodline&quot;.<br /> It'd need a The Pack equivalent first.</div> </div> </div> </div>PDFs are a really interesting way to go. It could definitely help increase output. I would love to see the Lodges mentioned in The Pack and the Legacies mentioned in the Awakening 2e corebook get updates. I confess, I have a skin in that game since I'm playing an Acanthus who is probably going to end up in the Walkers in Mist. <br /> <br /> Athanors completely changed between Created 1e and 2e. I would be interested to see some sort of translation of the 1e Athanors, which were basically the 1e z-splat, into a 2e context. I know constellations were sometimes given alchemical significance, especially in texts that identified the celestial bodies with different metals. But should the z-splat be a function of Lineage, or of Refinement? <br /> <br /> I also agree that Entitlements and Eldritch Orders need some updating, since the nature of Lost society has changed so much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T00:24:14-08:00","id":1008444,"title":"","content":"It would be fun to get to vote on which Z-Splats we get to see","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T09:20:08-08:00","id":1008576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1005543-z-splat-books?p=1008444#post1008444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would be fun to get to vote on which Z-Splats we get to see</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T10:01:59-08:00","id":1008587,"title":"","content":"Voting for Dark Eras was interesting, but I think didn't always work as well as it could have. I don't have any particular issues with any of the Dark Eras that were the product of voting, but a lot of cool ideas that came in second didn't seem to get a chance in later votes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T16:27:23-08:00","id":1008715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1005543-z-splat-books?p=1008587#post1008587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Voting for Dark Eras was interesting, but I think didn't always work as well as it could have. I don't have any particular issues with any of the Dark Eras that were the product of voting, but a lot of cool ideas that came in second didn't seem to get a chance in later votes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Too many good ideas, which is why we'll get a DE2. Yeah most of my complaints about the final product have nothing to do with the voting. Most were editorial in nature. DE isn't really the topic though.<br /> <br /> There are a lot of Z-Splats I'd like to see, but I have a few favorites. It'd be easy though to make a comprehensive list that we vote on of existing ones, and it'd be nice to have a few new. I wouldn't mind one Z-Splat book (per line), that ideally included how to make your own, of course merits/abilities, and as many splats as they can fit. After that of course I agree that I would prefer to sprinkle them about books that are more mixed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"